.TH RAND 1 "2026-05-22" "hako" "hako utilities"
.SH NAME
rand \- print a random integer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rand
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rand
prints a single random integer in the range [1, 100] to standard output,
followed by a newline.
The number is chosen using the operating system's cryptographically secure
random number generator.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
$ rand
42
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
Always exits 0.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hako (1)
